From 6f87e32fb84f6c89d1503ff278c0a564167854f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <noahc42@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:09:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Give each context its own rand() stream

rand() drew from one static Mersenne Twister shared by every context, so
contexts on different threads raced on it and one context's draws shifted
another's. The stream now lives in the compile context; rand nodes point at
it. Unseeded contexts start with Milkdrop's default seed (0x4141f00d), and
nodes built without a context fall back to a process-wide stream.

New API: projectm_eval_context_seed_rand(ctx, seed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
